# Cloudflare API Token for Akash Provider Integration
# ============================================================================
# NOTE: This file is OPTIONAL and for reference only
#
# The akash-cloudflare-integration module uses your existing cloudflared-token
# which already has all required permissions:
# - Zone:Read (read zone info)
# - DNS:Edit (create/update/delete DNS records)
# - Zone:Cache:Purge (purge cache for deployments)
#
# No new token is needed! The module defaults to: /run/agenix/cloudflared-token
#
# ============================================================================
# OPTIONAL: Create a dedicated token (only if you want to separate permissions)
# ============================================================================
# If you prefer to use a dedicated token for Akash integration (instead of
# sharing with cloudflared), follow these instructions:
#
# GENERATION INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Go to: https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
# 2. Click "Create Token"
# 3. Use template "Edit zone DNS" or custom permissions
# 4. Set permissions:
#    - Zone - DNS - Edit
#    - Zone - Zone - Read
#    - Zone - Cache Purge - Purge
# 5. Set zone resources to "Include" > "Specific zone" > reverb256.ca
# 6. Set TTL to "Never expire"
# 7. Copy token and encrypt with agenix:
#
#    agenix -e secrets/cloudflare-api-token.age
#
# 8. Paste token into the editor and save
#
# 9. Update module configuration to use the new token:
#
#    services.akash-cloudflare-integration = {
#      tokenFile = "/run/agenix/cloudflare-api-token";  # Use dedicated token
#    };
#
# ============================================================================
# TOKEN CONTENT (paste after running `agenix -e` command above)
# ============================================================================
